{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522031-w5-septs","id":1522031,"title":"W5 Septs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-03T21:34:15-07:00","id":1522031,"title":"W5 Septs","content":"So I am in the process of creating a w5 Sept and I am a little confused. In the previous editions Caerns are generally guarded by a Sept. Reading this multiple times I am getting that Caerns are as well in W5 but they can be protected by a single pack. Then I find Caern points that can be purchased by players to increase the power of their caern. Does this mean that when creating the caern I should note what the caern has when the PC's are introduced to the Caern and just allow them to build it from there? If I have three packs (not including the PC's) already in the Sept, do they have positions similar to how they did in previous editions or are these just packs taking turns guarding and caring for the Caern. Before they generally had packs that essentially lived at the caern and performed their duties. I was just curious how others were handling this..<br /> Has anyone thought about handing out a fresh Caern right after their rite of passage for the players pack to care for? Although this intrigues me I still find it difficult to wrap my head around how a new pack could handle such responsibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1070-cgunning","name":"cgunning","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T02:08:29-07:00","id":1522041,"title":"","content":"This is a bit tricky because I think the Caern-Trait-system has an issue. It says that with each Caern-level you gain one Caern-Trait but then in the Caern-Traits you got stuff like &quot;Well-Hidden&quot; where it says the trait can be taken multiple times. So that would mean a caern with a caern-level of 5 (which would represent caerns of global importance according to the book) would only have five Traits. After all, you pay for the increase in caern-value. There's no way to buy caern-Traits outright. But that low number of Traits doesn't really make sense to me. Especially with how many Traits say &quot;You can take this Trait multiple times.&quot;.<br /> <br /> The next thing is that there are two Rites needed that are connected to managing a caern (each Rite costs 5 XP unless it's picked at character creation). Your PC-group needs the Rite of the Living Caern (which needs to be performed monthly) and the Rite of the Caern-Building (you awaken the caern with that and use this Rite to increase the caern-value). As the difficulty for these Rites increases with the caern-value you need to have more Garou than just the PC-group participate in the Rite. Of course, with the way the Rite-mechanics work once you get to that point both Rites will cause a couple of complications each time they're performed because each Brutal Outcome creates a complication (like a spirit getting angry or attracting the attention of a Fenrir-pack in the area... stuff like that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does this mean that when creating the caern I should note what the caern has when the PC's are introduced to the Caern and just allow them to build it from there? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but be aware of the Difficulty that come from the caern-value as the two Rites mentioned above are conducted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I have three packs (not including the PC's) already in the Sept, do they have positions similar to how they did in previous editions or are these just packs taking turns guarding and caring for the Caern. </div> </div> </div>Well, the W5-book does mention a &quot;Master of the Howl&quot; which is something from the previous editions, so I guess you can just look at how previous editions handled that. The W5 book doesn't go into any sort of detail on that, of course, so I think that's the best course of action for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has anyone thought about handing out a fresh Caern right after their rite of passage for the players pack to care for? </div> </div> </div>If you want them to just be associated with a caern, there's the caern-Merit on pg 97. Other than that, the game expects the PC-group to pony up the XP for the two Rites and the caern-value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}